{"type":"text","timestamp":1794325256384,"sessionID":"ses_e39e70e5effeCYI8DTCFFfI5ZZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c61e98ad001CI5X5ixI3qEAxU","messageID":"msg_1c61e874f001FVoGG8TbKfHqgp","sessionID":"ses_e39e70e5effeCYI8DTCFFfI5ZZ","type":"text","text":"<think>Tailwind utilities are generated.\n\nNow let me think about whether I should test the frontend in a real browser. Let me check if there's a headless chrome / playwright available in the sandbox.\n\nActually, a simpler sanity check: use node to render? Not practical. Let me at least check that the JS bundle has no syntax errors by running `node --check`? It's an ES module bundle; `node --input-type=module --check` might work. Actually `node --check` works on scripts; for ESM I can use `node --input-type=module -e \"...\"`. Let me just try parsing with node's `--check` on the file (it may fail due to import statements in CJS mode). Let me try `node --experimental-vm-modules`? Simpler: the build succeeded, so syntax is valid (esbuild parsed it). Runtime errors are still possible.\n\nLet me check if a browser is available for a smoke test.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794325256365,"end":1794325256380}}}
