{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794325263629,"sessionID":"ses_e39e70e5effeCYI8DTCFFfI5ZZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c61eb4f0001m241Mc50vna0sV","messageID":"msg_1c61e9def001QPkpBplTEIKZp1","sessionID":"ses_e39e70e5effeCYI8DTCFFfI5ZZ","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794325263629,"sessionID":"ses_e39e70e5effeCYI8DTCFFfI5ZZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c61eb4f20019N03dAs6K4nqeO","messageID":"msg_1c61e9def001QPkpBplTEIKZp1","sessionID":"ses_e39e70e5effeCYI8DTCFFfI5ZZ","type":"text","text":"<think>No browser available. I'll rely on careful code review of the React app.\n\nLet me re-read my frontend code for runtime issues:\n\n1. `AuthPage`: `useAuth()` destructures `{ user, signIn, signUp }` ✓. It calls `signIn`/`signUp` from auth.tsx ✓.\n\n2. In auth.tsx `signIn`: calls apiLogin → writeToken → apiMe → setUser ✓.\n\n3. `PublicStatsPage`: uses `Link` import ✓ (used for the \"Sign in to the console\" button) ✓.\n\n4. `SubscriptionsPage`: \n   - `useMemo` imported ✓ used for rows.\n   - `Subscription` type imported and used in the map annotation ✓.\n   - `STATUS_LABELS`, `STATUS_ORDER` imported ✓.\n   - `apiPlans` imported ✓.\n   - Tabs: `const TABS: { value: \"\" | SubscriptionStatus; label: string }[]` — the spread `...STATUS_ORDER.map((status) => ({ value: status as \"\" | SubscriptionStatus, label: STATUS_LABELS[status] }))` ✓ typechecks (it passed tsc).\n   - `data.page_size` ✓.\n   \n5. `SubscriptionDetailPage`: imports `apiCreateInvoice, apiInvoices, apiRecordCollection, apiSubscription, apiUpdateSubscription` ✓; `STATUS_LABELS, STATUS_ORDER` ✓; `Invoice, Subscription, SubscriptionStatus` types ✓; `formatDate, formatDateTime, formatMoney` ✓; `StatusBadge` ✓.\n\nAll good — tsc passed with noUnusedLocals, which would have caught unused imports.\n\nNow let me think about the Docker build. The Dockerfile:\n```\nCOPY frontend/package.json frontend/package-lock.json* frontend/\nRUN cd frontend && (npm ci if lock exists)\nCOPY frontend/ frontend/\nRUN cd frontend && npm run build\n```\n`npm ci` requires package-lock.json to be in sync with package.json. I ran `npm install` which updated the lock ✓. Let me verify `npm ci` works (it will be run in Docker). Let me test it locally in a temp copy... that requires network (npm cache is warm, so it should be OK).\n\nAlso the Dockerfile copies `frontend/` over — including node_modules? .dockerignore excludes **/node_modules ✓.\n\nLet me verify `npm ci` works and then run the full Docker build if docker is available.\n\nLet me check for docker.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794325263602,"end":1794325263626}}}
