{"type":"text","timestamp":1794325267516,"sessionID":"ses_e39e70e5effeCYI8DTCFFfI5ZZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c61ec429001lcwl23e78jWm30","messageID":"msg_1c61eb525001QZGAbMzgJme9AP","sessionID":"ses_e39e70e5effeCYI8DTCFFfI5ZZ","type":"text","text":"<think>No docker available in the sandbox. But I can simulate the Docker build steps:\n1. `npm ci` in a fresh copy of frontend/ (without node_modules) → then `npm run build`.\n2. `pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock` → verify it resolves with the constraints (my backend only uses flask + stdlib, so no new deps — good, I didn't add any dependency).\n\nLet me verify pip install with constraints works (the lock file only lists flask/gunicorn deps). My app uses only Flask + stdlib ✓ — no changes to requirements.txt needed.\n\nLet me test `npm ci` in a temp dir.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794325267497,"end":1794325267513}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794325269949,"sessionID":"ses_e39e70e5effeCYI8DTCFFfI5ZZ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_wvhBVrrdmCbE9HrHMCiKz3Np","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rm -rf /workspace/.tmp/fe && mkdir -p /workspace/.tmp/fe && cp /workspace/frontend/package.json /workspace/frontend/package-lock.json /workspace/.tmp/fe/ && cd /workspace/.tmp/fe && npm ci --no-audit --no-fund 2>&1 | tail -5","timeout":300000},"output":"\nadded 43 packages in 2s\n","metadata":{"output":"\nadded 43 packages in 2s\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"rm -rf /workspace/.tmp/fe && mkdir -p /workspace/.tmp/fe && cp /workspace/frontend/package.json /workspace/frontend/package-lock.json /workspace/.tmp/fe/ && cd /workspace/.tmp/fe && npm ci --no-audit --no-fund 2>&1 | tail -5","time":{"start":1794325267506,"end":1794325269933}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c61ec42c001gPUs3c3LKB4HMG","sessionID":"ses_e39e70e5effeCYI8DTCFFfI5ZZ","messageID":"msg_1c61eb525001QZGAbMzgJme9AP"}}
